[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_vgim8")
fish_name = "Britfish"
grade = 1
sprite = ExtResource("2_c6gco")
catch_blurb = "Tastes like breakfast."
description = "British fisherfolk from Earth once anchored their galactic fleet in Pollywood’s orbit. They caught as many unique species of fish as they could with the hopes of adding them to their aquarium back in London. Apparently, only the common Pollywood Trout survived the voyage, and was sorry that it did. After undergoing genetic alteration and a series of “finishing schools” (originally misunderstood as “fishing schools”), the now-Britfish was sneakily returned to Pollywood with an ingrown top hat and tea cup. Somehow, a new top hat and tea cup eventually finds its way to all Britfish progeny.

While the Britfish reproduce at the same rate as the Pollywood Trout, you should not hope to catch the latter—it was taught in finishing school that one must always bite a hook if one is offered. Pollywood Trout simply lack that same etiquette. Another consequence of their finishing school is that although Britfish are the only known species capable of breaking through a Druyip Man o’ War’s formation, they insist that it is “unbecoming” to do so.

An interesting quality of Britfish is that they can be boiled in a kettle to extract a rich, tea-like flavor from their skin. Additionally, their meat tastes like a crispy baked good, and their eyes like beans. Nobody is too sure why this resulted from the genetic alterations.
"
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://cr3nmjdvpgh0a"
